// §5 "Worth knowing". Same job as every sibling's version of this block: make
// the reader distrust the cheapest quote without making a claim about TLB.
// The lever here is that the cheap method looks identical on the day.
const worthKnowingBody: TextBlockBody[] = [
  'A bad carpet clean and a good one look the same when the van drives away. The difference shows up about three weeks later. Over-wetting leaves moisture down in the backing, and on this coast, in a humid February, that is how you get a smell that will not shift and mould underneath a carpet that looks perfectly fine from above. Too much detergent left behind is a slower problem: it stays tacky, grabs the next lot of dirt, and the traffic lanes come back darker than they were before you paid to have them cleaned.',
  'So the question worth asking any carpet cleaner is not the price per room. It is what they do about drying, what they will do differently on a wool rug, and whether they will tell you before they start that a mark is permanent. We would rather lose the job than shrink your rug, and we would rather say a stain is staying than take your money and hope.',
];

